 hashtag#DevOps Interview Preparation Questions (4–8 Years Experience)

If you’re preparing for interviews with 4–8 years of experience, expect questions that go beyond basics and test real-world problem-solving, design decisions, and ownership.

Here are some must-prepare interview questions 👇

🔧 Technical & Hands-On

How do you design a highly available and scalable system on AWS?

Explain a CI/CD pipeline you built end-to-end. What challenges did you face?

How do you manage Infrastructure as Code and handle state files?

What’s your approach to zero-downtime deployments?

How do you monitor applications and infrastructure in production?

How do you troubleshoot a production outage under pressure?

Explain Docker vs Kubernetes and when to use each.

How do you handle secrets management in cloud environments?

☁️ Cloud & Architecture

How do you secure AWS resources using IAM best practices?

How do you design for cost optimization in AWS?
Difference between ALB, NLB, and ELB with use cases

How do you manage multi-region or multi-account AWS setups?

Explain auto-scaling strategies you have implemented

🧠 DevOps & Process

How do you collaborate with developers to improve deployment efficiency?

Describe a time you automated a manual process—what was the impact?

How do you handle rollbacks when deployments fail?

What DevOps metrics do you track? (DORA metrics, SLIs/SLOs)

How do you ensure security and compliance in CI/CD pipelines?

🎯 Scenario-Based (Very Important)

Production is down—what are your step-by-step actions?

How would you migrate an on-prem application to AWS?

How do you handle legacy systems in a modern DevOps setup?

How do you mentor junior engineers on your team?

⭐ Pro Tip

Interviewers at this level look for ownership, decision-making, and impact, not just tools.
